chore: developer-facing cleanup + GitHub Pages workflow

Removes
- Orbit v1.4 design.md at repo root. Was a stale closed-product
  spec leaking internal backend (Supabase) and host (Vercel)
  references. Not relevant to the open-source build.

CLAUDE.md (developer guide)
- Rewritten end-to-end on the current architecture.
- Documents Paper Deck identity primitives + sonata alias chain.
- Sections added: keyboard mode, Media Session, Wake Lock, CSP,
  Pod (Vault) persistent library, common mistakes table updated.
- Removed all references to the old "Midnight Purple / Silver
  Lavender" theme names and to the closed product line.

README.md
- New "What Origins We Contact" table (Google Fonts, YouTube
  nocookie, ytimg) — makes CSP whitelist visible to users.
- New "Keyboard Shortcuts" section.
- New "Identity" section describing Paper Deck primitives.

updatesData.ts changelog
- Theme entry no longer names the retired internal palettes.

GitHub Pages
- .github/workflows/pages.yml: build + deploy dist/ to Pages on
  push to main. Uses actions/checkout, setup-node 20, npm ci,
  type-check, build, upload-pages-artifact, deploy-pages.
  Requires Pages enabled in repo Settings (source: GitHub Actions).

Acceptance: tsc --noEmit exit 0; npm run build exit 0;
grep for leverage strings clean (LICENSE FSF refs allowed).
